NOTICE — scope of this license

The MIT license above covers the **source code** of this repository only
(the editor UI, the in-browser engine, the Python engine and the tools). It
does NOT cover the following, which have their own terms. See
`THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md` and `voicebanks/leapsinger_ja_3singer/README.md`.

  - The trained models and the voicebank shipped in `voicebanks/` and
    `vocoders/` (the acoustic model, the F0 and consonant-duration models, the
    breath bank, and the NHVSing vocoder). They are provided for personal,
    non-commercial use only, and **may not be redistributed**: they were
    trained on singing-voice databases (Oniku Kurumi, Natsume Yuuri, Namine
    Ritsu) whose terms of use bind every model made from them. Keep the
    credits, and for Natsume Yuuri the bundled terms of use
    (`voicebanks/leapsinger_ja_3singer/夏目悠李_利用規約.txt`), with anything
    you make from them.

  - The growl effect (`engine/voiceparams.py` `growl()` and its TypeScript
    port in `ui/src/engine-web/voiceparams.ts`), which follows
    hifisampler's `util/growl.py` (Apache License, Version 2.0; full text in
    `LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt`).

  - onnxruntime-web, which the browser engine loads at run time from jsDelivr
    (MIT, Microsoft).
